# Intent: a music session starts with the head nodding up and down on the beat, for a while, before the full dance (owner 2026-11-14: "nodding is up and down and that should probably go for a little bit before jumping into the more involved dancing where it looks everywhere and has lights on"; "ideally it would start head bobbing immediately to the beat"). BeatSwayModifier gets a bob-only mode: pitch up and down on every beat (every second beat above about 133 BPM), no side to side, no eye changes; it keeps the last known beat, or 600 ms, when the beat is unclear. self.robot.dance takes the name "bob" (the host asks for it at the nod), maipai_music_bob_start() is the unit's own offline nod, and the unit's session waits 15 s from the nod to the full dance (was 4 s).
# Upstream: MaiPai only (beat_sway.h, hal_mcp.cpp, hal_music.cpp, maipai_music_judge.h). Applies after 130.
# Check after a flash: play music: after about 3 s the head nods up and down in time; after about 15 s it changes to the full dance.
